WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:07.100
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Video audits what a film says.

1
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.362
Every number a film shows,
held against the code that decides it.

2
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:17.780
This suite told viewers it had
127 chart kinds. It had 167.

3
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.340
Prose in a README gets re-read.
A number in a keyframe does not.

4
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.727
Months of it, baked into every cut,
with nothing anywhere watching.

5
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.912
So the claims moved out of the film,
into a file that sits beside it.

6
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.920
A claim is a pair. The sentence on screen.
The file that settles it.

7
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.537
Verify reads that file.
It says whether the line is still true.

8
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.720
If the file has moved, the check fails.
It never quietly passes.

9
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.600
The dangerous number is
the one nobody declared.

10
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.940
A declared one names a file.
A number on screen names nothing.

11
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.500
So the scan reads the composition itself,
for numbers no claim covers.

12
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.199
The source is this repository's history,
where 127 survived for months.

13
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.740
Now point that scan at this film.

14
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.420
The declared ones come off the code.
One number is left over.

15
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.062
The only number it cannot
declare is the one it is about.

16
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.580
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
